  "content": {
    "id": "p20-q5-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "5",
    "prompt": "Draw a diagram of a triangle $ABC$ with a point $P$ on $AB$ and a point $Q$ on $AC$ such that $AP=12$, $PB=9$, $AQ=4$ and $QC=3$. Prove that $PQ\\parallel BC$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$PQ\\parallel BC$.",
      "worked": "The complete sides are $AB=12+9=21$ and $AC=4+3=7$. Thus $\\frac{AP}{AB}=\\frac{12}{21}=\\frac{4}{7}$ and $\\frac{AQ}{AC}=\\frac{4}{7}$. The included angle PAQ is the common angle BAC, so $\\triangle APQ\\sim\\triangle ABC$ by SAS. Corresponding angles give $\\angle APQ=\\angle ABC$, so $PQ\\parallel BC$ by the converse corresponding-angle property.",
